course: dictionary
lesson: 10327
title: Tragedy: sad events and sad plays
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A tragedy is a very sad event that causes great suffering, damage or death, like a terrible accident or disaster. Newspapers and history books use the word this way, and people remember tragedies with respect.
explain: The word also names a serious play or story that ends sadly, often with the death of the main character. Shakespeare's Romeo and Juliet is a famous example. Context helps you spot which meaning is used: «The Greeks invented theatre, with comedies and tragedies performed in great open-air theatres by actors wearing masks.» Comedies and tragedies are two kinds of drama, so here a tragedy is a play.
explain: Sometimes people joke, «What a tragedy!», about something small, like dropping an ice cream. This is informal and not really serious. To check the meaning, swap your idea into the sentence: if a flood destroys a town, «tragedy» fits; if an ice cream falls, it only fits as a joke.
fact: Tragedy is a noun. One is a tragedy, and more than one is tragedies.
fact: «Tragedy» means a very sad event that causes great suffering, damage or death.
fact: «Tragedy» can also mean a serious play or story that ends sadly, such as Romeo and Juliet.
fact: «Tragedy» can be used jokingly for something small that seems sad, like dropping your ice cream.
fact: Useful phrases: «a terrible tragedy», «end in tragedy», «tragedy struck». «The tragedy of the commons» describes how a shared thing, like a field, is ruined when everyone uses it only for themselves.
exercise: «The Greeks invented theatre, with comedies and tragedies performed in great open-air theatres by actors wearing masks.» In this sentence, what is a tragedy? | A loud noise made by the crowd | A type of mask worn by actors | A kind of dance performed at festivals | *A serious play or story that ends sadly
exercise: Which of these is a real tragedy, not a joke? | *A flood that destroys homes and takes lives | Dropping your ice cream on the way home | Losing a game of cards | Forgetting your homework at school
exercise: Find and copy one word from the Greek sentence that names a kind of happy play. | theatre | masks | actors | *comedies
test: «Romeo and Juliet» is a Shakespearean tragedy. What does this tell you about how the story ends? | Happily, with a big party | *Sadly, often with the death of the main characters | It is a comedy full of jokes | It has no ending at all
test: «The tragedy of the commons» is when everyone uses a shared thing for themselves until it is ruined for all. What is the main idea? | Shared things last forever, whatever people do | Only one person should ever use a shared thing | Playing games together is always a tragedy | *A shared thing gets ruined when everyone takes too much for themselves
exam: Read the sentence: «The tragedy struck when the bridge collapsed, and many people were hurt.» What does tragedy mean here? | *A very sad event that causes great suffering or damage | Something small and funny | A type of stage mask | A serious play that ends happily
